{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Regular Local Ring.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Regular Local Ring.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"regular local ring regular local ring","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Regular Local Ring.md","fileName":"Regular Local Ring.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Regular Local Ring","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:15\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Regular Sequences and Syzygies]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regular Sequences and Syzygies","Residue Field","Regular System of Parameters","Projective Dimension","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Regular Local Ring.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Regular Local Ring.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"regular local ring regular local ring","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Regular Local Ring.md","fileName":"Regular Local Ring.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Regular Local Ring","heading":"Regular Local Ring","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A Noetherian local ring (R,m,K) is regular when its Krull dimension equals the vector-space dimension of m/m² over the [[Residue Field]] K. Equivalently, the maximal ideal needs exactly dim(R) generators.\n\nThose generators form a [[Regular System of Parameters]]. The homological characterization says R is regular exactly when its residue field has finite [[Projective Dimension]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regular Sequences and Syzygies","Residue Field","Regular System of Parameters","Projective Dimension","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Regular Local Ring.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Regular Local Ring.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"regular local ring regular loc